	I bumped into one in my last ascension, too, actually. I was XL
28 or 29 at that point (eventually ascended at XL 30). It showed up in
the back hall of the Castle on my way down the dungeon to crack Rodney's
tower. I spammed charm monster at it until I tamed it... this is rather
more painful when chaotic than when lawful, but I got it eventually. I
can no longer say that I've never seen an Archon on the Astral, but this
time it was only because I brought it with me.

	(Incidentally, I *highly* recommend having three celestials with
artifact weapons and a hasted riding jabberwock covering your escape
route when raiding the Sanctum.)

	Your experience level *does* make a difference as to whether you
can meet Archons before you perform the Invocation. They don't spawn in
Gehennom, and you need to be fairly high level to meet them above the
Valley. Vlad's Tower is not technically part of Gehennom, though, and
it's deep enough that you can meet them there even at moderate levels.
Once you've performed the Invocation, though, the monster generation
changes - everything is based off the Sanctum depth rather than the
dungeon level you're actually on - so you have to be really low level to
avoid the possibility of Archon generation. With a deep Sanctum, it may
actually be impossible, even if you drain yourself down to XL 1.

